WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.810
On a December afternoon in 1891, a young Canadian

2
00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:08.037
instructor nailed two peach baskets to the balcony rails of

3
00:00:08.037 --> 00:00:12.908
a Springfield gymnasium and handed his restless students a new game.

4
00:00:13.258 --> 00:00:16.625
He had invented basketball — and he was not yet an American.

5
00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:19.739
He wrote out thirteen rules, asked a janitor for

6
00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:22.734
two boxes, and was handed two peach baskets instead.

7
00:00:23.084 --> 00:00:26.961
He filed for American citizenship near the end of the First World

8
00:00:26.961 --> 00:00:30.718
War, and the grant came in 1925 — when he was sixty-three years

9
00:00:30.718 --> 00:00:34.833
old and had been teaching in the country for more than three decades.

10
00:00:35.183 --> 00:00:37.828
The man who gave America one of its signature games

11
00:00:37.828 --> 00:00:40.628
spent most of his American life as a foreign national.

12
00:00:40.978 --> 00:00:44.380
